Value Required VRF (\S+)
Value GATEWAY (\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)

Start
  ^VRF:\s+${VRF}\s*$$
  ^Gateway of last resort is ${GATEWAY} to network 0\.0\.0\.0\s*$$ -> Record

# A trailing "VRF:" line with no default route (the common case — most VRFs
# on this fleet have none) would otherwise cause gotextfsm's implicit
# end-of-input Record to emit one bogus trailing record with an empty
# GATEWAY. This explicit, empty EOF state suppresses that.
#
# VRF is marked Required so a Gateway line encountered with no preceding
# VRF: line (truncated/partial output, a mid-stream reconnect) skips the
# record entirely (gotextfsm's onAppendRecord returns SKIP_RECORD for an
# empty Required value) instead of emitting one with VRF="" — which would
# otherwise flow into a malformed "show route vrf  summary" command.
EOF
